{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"certifiable":true,"criteria":[{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":273,"line_start":236,"path":"scripts/mutation_sandbox.py"},"criterion":"The `CI`-keyed fail-open branch is REMOVED from `wrap()`, together with its now sole-purpose helper `_ci_environment()` — leaving the helper would be dead code whose docstring argues FOR the behaviour just deleted. Ambient `CI` alone can no longer disable the sandbox. Verified by a test asserting that with `CI` truthy, no mechanism, and no opt-out, `wrap()` raises `SandboxUnavailable`.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":699,"line_start":659,"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py"},"criterion":"The tests that asserted the removed behaviour are removed or inverted, not left asserting a contract that no longer exists: `test_ci_runner_proceeds_unsandboxed_with_a_warning` (inverted), `test_falsey_ci_values_do_not_waive_the_sandbox` (subsumed), `test_the_ci_fail_open_warning_names_the_variable_and_its_value` (removed). `test_workstation_still_aborts_when_no_sandbox` and `test_a_working_sandbox_is_used_even_on_ci` remain meaningful and stay.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":286,"line_start":276,"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py"},"criterion":"`REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED` remains the single waiver, unchanged in name and semantics. No second opt-in surface is introduced. Verified by a test that the opt-out still permits an unsandboxed run and still logs at WARNING.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":155,"line_start":118,"path":".github/workflows/_mutation.yml"},"criterion":"`.github/workflows/_mutation.yml` sets the explicit opt-out, with a comment stating that the gate runs UNSANDBOXED there and why, so the exposure is visible in a reviewed file rather than implied by an ambient variable. Its stale 'fails CLOSED' comment is corrected.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":153,"line_start":144,"path":"docs/local-dev-env.md"},"criterion":"`docs/local-dev-env.md` no longer describes a CI fallback that does not exist.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":73,"line_start":64,"path":"tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py"},"criterion":"Every other lane is checked for reliance on the removed branch and shown not to need it: the enforcement lane has a working `bwrap` (`0d22-f664`), macOS cells have `sandbox-exec`, and the pytest cells only run `@live` tests that skip without a mechanism. Verified by naming each lane and its mechanism.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":267,"line_start":248,"path":"scripts/mutation_sandbox.py"},"criterion":"Bug 'Ambient CI alone can disable the mutation sandbox' is actually resolved: the reported defect no longer reproduces and expected behavior holds.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true}],"findings":[],"material_fingerprint":null,"metrics":{"alias_index_build_ms":1132,"commits_inspected":2832,"descendant_ids":0,"descendant_scope_ms":3559,"det_ms":4715.0,"diff_validation_ms":229,"distinct_references":2365,"git_history_read_ms":115,"landing_check_ms":1506,"llm_calls":1,"llm_ms":109176.2,"material_policy_ms":0,"pre_verifier_total_ms":11442,"referencing_commits_found":2,"requests":19,"structural_scan_ms":6055,"ticket_ref_resolution_ms":24,"tool_calls":18,"total_ms":113942.7,"verifier_annotation_ms":0,"verifier_attempt_count":1,"verifier_attempt_setup_ms":1,"verifier_attempts_ms":275734,"verifier_between_attempts_ms":0,"verifier_build_drift_ms":777,"verifier_call_ms":275757,"verifier_code_snapshot_ms":112,"v